## Summary

After a user starts Half-Speed Playback and manually stops it, ordinary Play still plays at half speed. The previous alternate playback rate survives the Stop/Play transition. This also affects loop playback, where completing a loop does not clear the rate. Users can recover by letting a finite non-looped selection finish or by reconnecting the audio device, but ordinary Stop followed by Play does not restore normal playback.

## Runtime or environment

Source baseline: `storytold/soundcraft` commit `d7fc5dc383837b1059ee984cd535eb745dabaee7`. Verification used static source proof only. No GUI, live app, audio device, or runtime reproduction was run. The affected path requires an app with a functioning `Player`; the no-player transport simulation is outside this proof.

## Steps to reproduce

These steps were traced in source and were not executed. Use the desktop app with its synthesized demo session, an active output Player, and no record-armed or input-monitored tracks. The demo's session sample rate is 48,000 Hz. The example uses a one-second loop to avoid depending on how quickly the user presses Stop before a finite selection ends.

1. Through the running app's documented control protocol, send the following requests one at a time. Allow the app to process each request before sending the next. The first four requests establish a nonempty selection longer than the callback's 64-sample minimum and disable unrelated playback options.

```json
{"method":"engine.execute","params":{"command":"edit.select","params":{"start":0,"end":48000}}}
{"method":"engine.execute","params":{"command":"options.loop_playback","params":{"value":true}}}
{"method":"engine.execute","params":{"command":"options.pre_post_roll","params":{"value":false}}}
{"method":"engine.execute","params":{"command":"options.insertion_follows_playback","params":{"value":false}}}
{"method":"engine.execute","params":{"command":"transport.half_speed","params":{}}}
```

